  *      CFG and IN_OUT of the sensors' MCLK, reset and supply-switch pins and the CCI's
  *   4. only if titan_top is on and the CCI, CPAS AHB and SOC AHB clocks run: the CCI's version register
  * The result: kern.sweet_cam_status (text) and the console ("SWEET CAM:").
+ *
+ * Patch 3075b, step C2: kern.sweet_cam=2 (root) powers the rear main sensor (cam-sensor@0, a Sony IMX363), reads its chip
+ * ID and powers it down again. The sequence is the sensor's own (its CamX module file com.qti.sensormodule.imx363.bin of
+ * the phone's vendor partition, read by hand; NOTES "CAMERA C2"): up VANA 1 ms, CUSTOM1 high 1 ms, VIO 1 ms, VDIG 1 ms,
+ * RESET high 12 ms, MCLK 10 ms; down RESET low, VDIG, VIO, CUSTOM1 low, VANA, MCLK, 1 ms each. The rails as the live DT
+ * gives them: VANA = PM8998 L22 (also the OLED panel's vdda: NEVER voted or changed here; C2 only reads it and goes on if
+ * it is already on at 2.8-3.0 V) plus the VANA switch GPIO 12; CUSTOM1 = GPIO 40; VIO = camera_viodd_ldo's enable GPIO 75;
+ * VDIG = camera_vdig_ldo's enable GPIO 99 (the DT also names PM8998 GPIO 11 for VDIG: only read here); RESET = GPIO 119;
+ * MCLK = camcc MCLK0 on GPIO 13 (function cam_mclk, 4 mA), from the crystal at 19.2 MHz (the module asks 24 MHz, which
+ * needs camcc's PLL2; enough to read an ID), inside titan_top_gdsc (the sensors' cam_clk), after GCC's CAMERA_XO branch.
+ * The chip ID: slave 0x34 (8-bit), 2 bytes at register 0x0016, expected 0x0363, through the CCI master 0 pins (GPIO 17
+ * SDA, 18 SCL) driven by hand as open-drain GPIOs (~50 kHz) instead of the CCI block (HakiOS does the same on its POCO).
+ * Every pin is put back as it was found; the branch, the domain and GCC's XO only if this run switched them on.
  */
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
 #include <sys/param.h>
